From: Canaan K230 BSP <bsp@canaan-creative.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Nov 2026 07:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: canaan: vpu: honour per-plane data_offset on input
 frames

The VPU wants NV12 as two planes. A camera hands out NV12 as one buffer,
because that is all the V4L2 core allows it to do: v4l2_format_info()
gives V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12 mem_planes = 1, so one frame is one dmabuf and
there is no second fd to import.

V4L2 already has an answer for that - name the same fd on both planes
and set data_offset on the second one to the size of the luma. The
driver did not implement it, so the only way to feed the encoder from
the camera was to copy every frame into a buffer the driver did like.
At 1080p30 that is 3 MB of memcpy per frame, and the memory it reads
from is uncached.

Three things were in the way:

 - update_mvx_buffer() passed V4L2's bytesused straight through as MVX's
   'filled'. V4L2 counts data_offset inside bytesused, MVX does not; the
   driver's own comment in update_v4l2_bytesused() says so and the
   dequeue direction already obeys it. The queue direction therefore
   over-counted by data_offset and mvx_buffer_filled_set() rejected a
   plane that fit exactly.

 - Nothing kept data_offset for the firmware to use.

 - mvx_firmware_v2.c pointed plane_top at the start of the imported
   memory, so the chroma was read from the address of the luma and the
   picture came out green.

Fixed by carrying data_offset in a new field of struct
mvx_buffer_plane. The existing @offset field could not be reused: it
also carries the intra-page remainder of an mmap offset, which
mvx_buffer_va() has already accounted for, and mvx_buffer_frame_set()
clears it.

Deliberately inert for everyone who does not set data_offset, which is
every existing user - ffmpeg's v4l2_m2m encoder never writes it on QBUF.
With data_offset == 0 the subtraction, the new field and the added term
in plane_top are all zero and the driver behaves exactly as before.

Capture buffers clear the new field in mvx_buffer_frame_set(), next to
where @offset is already cleared, because vb2_fill_vb2_v4l2_buffer()
does not reset data_offset on a capture QBUF - what is left in there is
whatever the driver itself reported on the previous dequeue.

Signed-off-by: Canaan K230 BSP <bsp@canaan-creative.com>
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/canaan/vpu/mvx_buffer.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/canaan/vpu/mvx_buffer.h
@@ -61,6 +61,20 @@
 	unsigned int stride;
 	unsigned int filled;
 	unsigned int offset;
+	/**
+	 * data_offset: Where this plane's data starts inside the memory it was
+	 * imported from, taken straight from v4l2_plane.data_offset.
+	 *
+	 * Zero for every caller that gives each plane memory of its own, which
+	 * is all of them except an application that hands in one dmabuf
+	 * holding a whole multi-plane frame - the chroma of an NV12 frame
+	 * being the same dmabuf, luma_size bytes in.
+	 *
+	 * Kept apart from @offset on purpose. @offset also carries the
+	 * intra-page remainder of an mmap offset and is cleared again for
+	 * capture buffers, so it cannot be reused for this.
+	 */
+	unsigned int data_offset;
 	unsigned int afbc_width;
 };
 
--- a/drivers/media/platform/canaan/vpu/mvx_v4l2_buffer.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/canaan/vpu/mvx_v4l2_buffer.c
@@ -316,7 +316,9 @@
 	mvx_buf->user_data = vb2->timestamp;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < vb2->num_planes; i++) {
-		unsigned int offset = vb2->planes[i].data_offset;
+		unsigned int data_offset = vb2->planes[i].data_offset;
+		unsigned int filled = vb2->planes[i].bytesused;
+		unsigned int offset = data_offset;
 
 			/*
 			 * For single planar mmap buffers the offset is carried by
@@ -325,8 +327,34 @@
 		if (vb2->memory == V4L2_MEMORY_MMAP)
 			offset += vb2->planes[i].m.offset & ~PAGE_MASK;
 
-		ret = mvx_buffer_filled_set(mvx_buf, i,
-					    vb2->planes[i].bytesused, offset);
+		/*
+		 * V4L2 counts data_offset inside bytesused, MVX does not -
+		 * see the comment in update_v4l2_bytesused() below, which
+		 * hands the pair back the other way round as
+		 * 'filled + offset'. Take it off here so the two agree.
+		 *
+		 * Without this a plane that starts part way into its buffer,
+		 * which is how one allocation carries both the luma and the
+		 * chroma of an NV12 frame, is rejected by
+		 * mvx_buffer_filled_set() for overflowing a buffer it fits
+		 * in exactly.
+		 *
+		 * Everyone who leaves data_offset at zero, which is every
+		 * caller that gives each plane memory of its own, is left
+		 * exactly where they were.
+		 */
+		if (filled >= data_offset)
+			filled -= data_offset;
+
+		/*
+		 * Remembered separately for the firmware, which has to be
+		 * told where the plane starts. It cannot read it back out of
+		 * @offset: that one also carries the intra-page remainder
+		 * added just above, and mvx_buffer_frame_set() clears it.
+		 */
+		mvx_buf->planes[i].data_offset = data_offset;
+
+		ret = mvx_buffer_filled_set(mvx_buf, i, filled, offset);
 		if (ret != 0)
 			return ret;
 	}
--- a/drivers/media/platform/canaan/vpu/mvx_buffer.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/canaan/vpu/mvx_buffer.c
@@ -478,6 +478,17 @@
 		if (buf->dir == MVX_DIR_OUTPUT) {
 			int ret;
 
+			/*
+			 * A capture frame is laid out by the driver, every
+			 * plane starting at the top of its own memory. Clear
+			 * the offset the application sent in, the same way
+			 * @offset is cleared just above - vb2 does not reset
+			 * data_offset on a capture QBUF, so what is left
+			 * there is whatever the driver itself reported on the
+			 * previous dequeue.
+			 */
+			plane->data_offset = 0;
+
 			ret = mvx_buffer_filled_set(buf, i, size[i], 0);
 			if (ret != 0)
 				return ret;
--- a/drivers/media/platform/canaan/vpu/mvx_firmware_v2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/canaan/vpu/mvx_firmware_v2.c
@@ -1328,8 +1328,17 @@
 		for (i = 0; i < buf->nplanes; i++) {
 			struct mvx_buffer_plane *plane = &buf->planes[i];
 
+			/*
+			 * plane->data_offset is where this plane starts
+			 * inside the memory it was imported from. It is zero
+			 * for every caller that gives each plane memory of
+			 * its own, and it is what lets one allocation carry a
+			 * whole NV12 frame: the chroma is the same dmabuf,
+			 * luma_size bytes in.
+			 */
 			if (plane->stride > 0)
-				planar->plane_top[i] = mvx_buffer_va(buf, i);
+				planar->plane_top[i] = mvx_buffer_va(buf, i) +
+						       plane->data_offset;
 
 			if (f.frame_flags & MVE_BUFFER_FRAME_FLAG_INTERLACE) {
 				// interlace mode
-- 
2.34.1

